                        "glosses": [
                            "A tube or tubular organ."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a8c6af28-a8c3-4405-a43b-4ee8cca6fcdc",
                                "sense_id": "04747bb3-d8ab-356e-9f02-a08258ffd81c",
                                "text": "Compared with skulls of darwini, skulls of andium are smaller with shorter tooth rows (fig. 13), have less globular bullae that taper more gradually to the tubae, and a shorter, proportionately narrower rostrum with nasals usually relatively blunt behind and seldom projecting posteriorly far behind the premaxillae (pl. 11)."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f5917c32-2ed0-3fdb-9aaa-8d6a8945eb47",
                        "entry_id": "f6b2706b-7d0b-3c04-b416-eebd2eb5b9a2",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A type of Roman military trumpet, distinct from the modern tuba."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "97f5ac4e-b2e1-428c-9841-91127c59e544",
                                "sense_id": "f5917c32-2ed0-3fdb-9aaa-8d6a8945eb47",
                                "text": "From the eleventh century onwards, the trumpets, which had till then been modelled on the Roman tubae with their straightforward and somewhat rough sound, began to grow longer and thinner as their bells widened."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bab73ac0-4a3b-45c6-bf2c-315fb16feed4",
                                "sense_id": "f5917c32-2ed0-3fdb-9aaa-8d6a8945eb47",
                                "text": "This depicts trumpet blowing angels gripping instruments, of the Roman tubae variety, halfway down with the right hand, the left hand covering their mouth and the mouthpiece."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2e59c0f5-c16f-40a5-a188-fde83cda2e08",
                                "sense_id": "f5917c32-2ed0-3fdb-9aaa-8d6a8945eb47",
                                "text": "As he drew nearer to Worms, he heard the brassy blare of Roman tubae from the ruddy sandstone walls of the city."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
